# Returning Early

You can have multiple `return` statements to exit a method early:

```csharp
float CalculateDamage(float baseDamage, bool isCritical)
{
    if (isCritical)
    {
        return baseDamage * 2f; // early return
    }
    return baseDamage; // normal return
}
```

The method stops executing as soon as it hits a `return`.

slides.codeSnippet:
Transform FindNearestEnemy()
{
    GameObject[] enemies = GameObject.FindGameObjectsWithTag("Enemy");
    Transform nearest = null;
    float minDist = Mathf.Infinity;

    foreach (GameObject enemy in enemies)
    {
        float dist = Vector3.Distance(transform.position, enemy.transform.position);
        if (dist < minDist)
        {
            minDist = dist;
            nearest = enemy.transform;
        }
    }
    return nearest;
}

